datasource_sql_semicolon: two statements separated by `;` in a SQL-mode
body (and a trailing `;`). The body runs as one SQL command and STARLIMS
rejects the document ("Invalid SQL statement: remove any misplaced
semicolons(;)"), so each separator reports an error. The header's own
terminators never flag.
-- input.ds --
:DSN := DATABASE;
:PARAMETERS nKeep := 30;

delete from scan_log where age_days > @nKeep;
update scan_counter set last_purge = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
-- format --
:DSN := DATABASE;
